# Agent primitives: text agents read as directives, and configuration they
# execute. Named explicitly rather than relying on the `*` wildcard above, so
# these survive any future relaxation of it. `.claude/settings.json` and its
# peers can define hooks that run shell commands, which is why the directories
# matter at least as much as the markdown.
AGENTS.md   @qwts
CLAUDE.md   @qwts
.claude/    @qwts
.codex/     @qwts
.cursor/    @qwts
.mcp.json   @qwts

# Shared skills distributed to the fleet. A skill is read as a directive and
# ships executable scripts alongside it, so it is the same class as the entries
# above — and higher blast radius, because it is installed into every agent's
# harness rather than scoped to one repository.
/skills/    @qwts